SUMMARY:Homeschool explorer day at Fort Morgan
DESCRIPTION:Gulf Coast Explorers runs a morning field programme at Fort Mo
 rgan\, the masonry fort that guarded the mouth of Mobile Bay and took the
  brunt of the Battle of Mobile Bay in 1864. The programme covers the fort
 's role in coastal defence and works through the cannons and the tunnels 
 rather than around them. It is built for grades 3 to 12\, and a parent or
  responsible adult has to come along. The operator books by request rathe
 r than selling seats\, so this one starts with an email.\nPrice: not publ
 ished by the venue\, so confirm before you go\nArea: Orange Beach & Gulf 
 Shores\nTimes: Friday 9/25 · 9:00 AM to 12:00 PM\nhttps://coastaleventur
 es.com/events/ev-homeschool-explorer-day-fort-morgan-and-mobi-0925.html
LOCATION:Fort Morgan State Historic Site\, 110 State Highway 180\, Gulf Sh
 ores\, AL 36542
